{
  "query": "How do I decide whether to use an updatable market or an immutable one?",
  "summary": "The choice is a trade-off between adaptability and trust minimization. Updatable markets let operators fix bugs, tune risk parameters, and respond to market changes. Immutable markets give users certainty that the rules cannot change after they deposit or borrow, but they cannot be patched or adjusted if something goes wrong. Your choice should depend on how much risk you can tolerate, how often you expect parameters to need changing, and how much your users value guarantees over flexibility.",
